 individuals who need to limit their potassium intake, as they contain high levels of potassium. Overall, legumes play a significant role in nutrition, but their consumption should be tailored to individual dietary needs, especially for those with specific health conditions.", "ÁNGEL MANUEL CARACUEL GARCÍA:Ángel Manuel Caracuel García is an author known for his work on the normalization of hospital food and nutrition.", "CAMPFRÍO FOOD GROUP:Campofrío Food Group is a food company that specializes in the production and distribution of processed meat products. In addition to its core business, the company has also published works on hospital nutrition and food standards, indicating its commitment to promoting health and quality in food consumption.", "DÍAZ DE SANTOS:Díaz de Santos is a prominent publishing company based in Spain, recognized for its extensive range of academic and professional publications. The company specializes in educational literature, with a particular focus on medical and nutritional topics. Among its notable works is the \"Manual de Nutrición Clínica y Dietética,\" which highlights its commitment to providing valuable resources in the field of nutrition. Overall, Díaz de Santos is well-regarded for its contributions to both academic and professional literature, particularly in the areas of health and education.", "NUTRITION UNIT:The Nutrition Unit is a department within hospitals responsible for overseeing dietary plans and ensuring they meet patients' nutritional needs.", "ONCOLOGICAL TREATMENT:Oncological treatment refers to medical care provided to patients with cancer, which may require specific dietary considerations.", "DIABETIC DEBUT:Diabetic debut refers to the initial onset of diabetes in a patient, during which dietary education and management are crucial.", "FOOD ALLERGIES:Food allergies are adverse reactions to certain foods that must be documented and managed in a hospital setting to ensure patient safety.", "NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTS:Nutritional supplements are additional nutrients provided to patients when their dietary intake is insufficient for their health needs. They are particularly recommended for patients post-bariatric surgery to ensure adequate protein and nutrient intake. These products are also intended to enhance the diet of individuals with specific health conditions, such as cancer and diabetes, to improve nutritional intake and support recovery. Nutritional supplements are commonly used in clinical settings for patients with specific nutritional needs, offering a means to provide essential vitamins, minerals, and trace elements that may be lacking in their regular diet. Overall, nutritional supplements play a crucial role in enhancing dietary intake and ensuring that individuals receive the necessary nutrients for optimal health.", "HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA:Hypercholesterolemia is a condition of elevated cholesterol levels in the blood, which may require dietary modifications.", "CARDIOVASCULAR ISSUES:Cardiovascular issues refer to health problems related to the heart and blood vessels, often requiring dietary adjustments.", "FOOD INTOLERANCES:Food intolerances refer to adverse reactions to specific foods that do not engage the immune system. These intolerances often require individuals to make dietary modifications to avoid discomfort and other related symptoms.", "CODES OF DIETS:Codes of diets are protocols established in hospitals that outline various dietary options available for patients.", "MANUAL DE NUTRICIÓN Y METABOLISMO:Manual de Nutrición y Metabolismo is a publication that provides comprehensive information on nutrition and metabolism."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}